    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0349" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg309"/>

                <head>Mr. F. W. Seward to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1350.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 12, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I transmit herewith a printed copy of three
                    proclamations of the 11th instant, made by the President of the United
                    States—one relating to the closing of certain ports of entry, another
                    supplementary thereunto and relating to the port of Key West, in Florida, and a
                    third relating to reciprocal hospitalities to the vessels of foreign navies in
                    the ports of the United States, and to vessels of the navy of the United States
                    in foreign ports. You will perceive by these proclamations that it is believed
                    that the time has arrived when the United States (whatever claim or pretence may
                    have existed heretofore to the contrary) are now entitled to claim the same
                    friendly rights and hospitalities for their naval vessels which they are willing
                    to concede to those of all maritime nations.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>





